    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 157,
        "text": "Hi, Ben. Thanks for helping me with the library survey report. I've got the numbers from last year and this year, but I'm not sure how to describe them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d1fdcdccb1f3c69b8e73b6acbaa0759b2862581d2e286f708c175328e607edeb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 163,
        "sourceEnd": 319,
        "text": "No problem. Let's look at the visitor numbers first. So, last year the library had 8,000 visitors, and this year it had 10,000. That's an increase of 2,000.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "4493ac5c66ad6d002c7ff48ea8e5966c6d58e917f5e8ccbb9213f81ff959e02d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 325,
        "sourceEnd": 417,
        "text": "Right. And the number of books borrowed? Last year it was 15,000, and this year it's 18,000.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "65f9e40c2c57d1658b083d4eea371a2026653db3ecacec6dc58eab72b3a3c028",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 423,
        "sourceEnd": 557,
        "text": "So that's a rise of 3,000. That's a 20 percent increase, isn't it? Wait, no. 3,000 divided by 15,000 is 0.2, so yes, 20 percent. Good.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "48bd60bca41e983021974be6921633a1ef5f0b1728616e599193cf82bc8153c3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 563,
        "sourceEnd": 699,
        "text": "OK. What about the number of events? Last year there were 40 events, and this year there were 50. So there was an increase of 10 events.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "11a22300ee30ed210ea52399bd81e90902bb0ff73413f9e8636bdf795f66f5c6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 705,
        "sourceEnd": 800,
        "text": "Yes, and attendance at events? Last year 600 people came, and this year 900. That's a big jump.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "aac25b7eb8588b9df25bbbbd0924138f5dc61c0b3b22c76067c98f0b662feb81",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 806,
        "sourceEnd": 935,
        "text": "It is. Now, the number of computers. Last year there were 20 computers, but this year there are only 15. So the number decreased.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "9bb6546389f16fe64da2c4a15ccd8942389f3b22a4a1ad01657ff62a9d7e155c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 941,
        "sourceEnd": 1096,
        "text": "That's a decrease of 5 computers. And the number of staff? Last year there were 8 staff members, and this year there are 10. So there was an increase of 2.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "7d08d5c6846cec19bf0f4a01cb968047c87d6b8e0da383fe9d45d5d091c2cbaa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1102,
        "sourceEnd": 1247,
        "text": "Right. And the opening hours? Last year the library was open 50 hours a week, and this year it's open 55 hours. So that's an increase of 5 hours.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3545e1041a4ae80a72506cc02cd882d85070cce96db32f75a3b56ad49a51d69e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1253,
        "sourceEnd": 1426,
        "text": "OK. Now, what about the satisfaction survey? Last year 70 percent of visitors were satisfied, and this year 85 percent were satisfied. So satisfaction went up by 15 percent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "94c332ee059c183e66b54694f840125adb8d088f008cb816616e4c5b3e4bf2a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1432,
        "sourceEnd": 1504,
        "text": "Wait, is that 15 percent or 15 percentage points? I always get confused.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "de29745f791508cd87f7180761a1c5a482961e4d02358be9ee46b7a46fec12bf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1510,
        "sourceEnd": 1810,
        "text": "Good question. It's 15 percentage points. The percentage went from 70 to 85, so that's a 15 percentage point increase. But if you say 'increased by 15 percent', that's not quite right because 15 percent of 70 is 10.5, so it would be 80.5 percent. So we should say 'increased by 15 percentage points'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "25524104fc3c2b805873cab3119efd110d4a585c2acfeb3162fb75381efa6e92",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1816,
        "sourceEnd": 1967,
        "text": "OK, I'll write that. And the number of new members? Last year there were 200 new members, and this year there were 250. So there was an increase of 50.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "aee4ca004cb06b33a1f878d2dc74b43ed20fe187745a469948c379c7d55c5a9b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1973,
        "sourceEnd": 2070,
        "text": "Yes. So overall, most numbers went up, but the number of computers went down. That's interesting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "09ab728d56154bd5aaf28664e93db5d7cb69b9d6585f586bc617887dea38efcf",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2076,
        "sourceEnd": 2128,
        "text": "It is. I think we have enough data now. Thanks, Ben!",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "aea8f38e461a963da9f719f18cbd72aacbdd7a1543e5e5aa32296794030234aa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
